.SH NAME
.PP
ws_detach - terminates WebSocket protocol and returns the underlying
socket
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IP
.nf
\f[C]
#include <libdill.h>

int ws_detach(
    int s,
    int status,
    const void* buf,
    size_t len,
    int64_t deadline);
\f[R]
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
\f[B]WARNING: This is experimental functionality and the API may change
in the future.\f[R]
.PP
WebSocket is a message-based protocol defined in RFC 6455.
It can be used as a bidirectional communication channel for
communication with a web server.
.PP
This function does the terminal WebSocket handshake and returns the
underlying socket to the user.
The socket is closed even in the case of error, except for
\f[B]EBUSY\f[R]: the socket is then left untouched for the coroutine
that is using it.
.PP
\f[B]s\f[R]: Handle of the WebSocket socket.
.PP
\f[B]status\f[R]: Status to send to the peer.
If set zero, no status will be sent.
.PP
\f[B]buf\f[R]: Message to send to the peer.
If set to NULL, no message will be sent.
Note that WebSocket protocol limits the sizeof the shutdown message to
125 bytes.
.PP
\f[B]len\f[R]: Size of the message to send to the peer, in bytes.
.PP
\f[B]deadline\f[R]: A point in time when the operation should time out,
in milliseconds.
Use the \f[B]now\f[R] function to get your current point in time.
0 means immediate timeout, i.e., perform the operation if possible or
return without blocking if not.
-1 means no deadline, i.e., the call will block forever if the operation
cannot be performed.
.PP
This function is not available if libdill is compiled with
\f[B]--disable-sockets\f[R] option.
.SH RETURN VALUE
.PP
In case of success the function returns underlying socket handle.
In case of error it returns -1 and sets \f[B]errno\f[R] to one of the
values below.
.SH ERRORS
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]EBADF\f[R]: Invalid handle.
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]EBUSY\f[R]: The handle is currently being used by a different
coroutine.
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]ECANCELED\f[R]: Current coroutine was canceled.
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]ECONNRESET\f[R]: Broken connection.
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]ENOTSUP\f[R]: The handle is not an WebSocket protocol handle.
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]ETIMEDOUT\f[R]: Deadline was reached.
.SH EXAMPLE
.IP
.nf
\f[C]
struct ipaddr addr;
ipaddr_remote(&addr, \[dq]www.example.org\[dq], 80, 0, -1);
int s = tcp_connect(&addr, -1);
s = ws_attach_client(s, \[dq]/\[dq], \[dq]www.example.org\[dq], WS_TEXT, -1);
ws_send(s, WS_TEXT, \[dq]Hello, world!\[dq], 13, -1);
int flags;
char buf[256];
ssize_t sz = ws_recv(s, &flags, buf, sizeof(buf), -1);
assert(flags & WS_TEXT);
s = ws_detach(s, -1);
tcp_close(s, -1);
\f[R]
.fi
